      <h2 id="update-checking-cluster-health_update-before-the-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Checking the cluster health<a href="#update-checking-cluster-health_update-before-the-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You should check the cluster health often during the update. Check for the node status, cluster Operators status and failed pods.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check the status of the cluster Operators by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get co"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                                       VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   DEGRADED   SINCE   MESSAGE\nauthentication                             4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\nbaremetal                                  4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\ncloud-controller-manager                   4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\ncloud-credential                           4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\ncluster-autoscaler                         4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\nconfig-operator                            4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\nconsole                                    4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\n...\nservice-ca                                 4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\nstorage                                    4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check the status of the cluster nodes:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE     VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready    control-plane,master   4d22h   v1.27.15+6147456\nctrl-plane-1   Ready    control-plane,master   4d22h   v1.27.15+6147456\nctrl-plane-2   Ready    control-plane,master   4d22h   v1.27.15+6147456\nworker-0       Ready    mcp-1,worker           4d22h   v1.27.15+6147456\nworker-1       Ready    mcp-2,worker           4d22h   v1.27.15+6147456"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check that there are no in-progress or failed pods. There should be no pods returned when you run the following command.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get po -A | grep -E -iv 'running|complete'"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
